5	 * @test @b movbe_l1d
6	 * @test @b movbe_l2
7	 * @parblock
8	 * Reload-path localization probes for core-179 SDC.
9	 *
10	 * Hypothesis: the 179 SDC lies in the per-core load data path (L1D read
11	 * array -> load port -> register), NOT in cross-core LLC/memory.  If so,
12	 * the defect should manifest only when the reload *hits* L1D; forcing the
13	 * reload to miss L1D (serve from L2/L3) should eliminate the SDC.
14	 *
15	 * Two SEPARATE tests (not one test with a branch), so neither hot loop
16	 * contains a regime-selection conditional that would perturb the instruction
17	 * schedule and silence the timing-sensitive defect (see memory
18	 * dump-variant-noremove-report-fail-verified — any hot-loop conditional
19	 * can break triggering).
20	 *
21	 *   - movbe_l1d: hot loop byte-identical to movbe_dump.cpp (ldr/rev/str/
22	 *     ldr/cmp).  Reload of input[i] hits L1D.  Expected: SDC triggers.
23	 *   - movbe_l2:  same ldr/rev/str/ldr/cmp, but the reload of input[i] is
24	 *     preceded by `dc civac` + dsb on input[i]'s address, evicting it from
25	 *     L1D so the reload fetches from L2/L3.  Expected (if hypothesis
26	 *     holds): SDC disappears.
27	 *
28	 * On miscompare, logs input/golden/actual/xor (same as movbe_dump) then
29	 * report_fail_msg (noreturn) — matching movbe_dump's behavior; one TEST_LOOP
30	 * pass already logs a batch of events before the thread is killed.
31	 * @endparblock
32	 */
